    "grade": "PASS",
    "ledger": [
      {
        "id": "E1",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "On the AI Infrastructure team at Ai2, we’re responsible for providing the institute’s GPU compute capacity, specifically targeting large, distributed training workloads.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/allenai/impactful-scheduling",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-09T15:20:29.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-11T12:28:11.769Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E2",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "At Ai2, we manage thousands of NVIDIA H100, B200, and B300 GPUs arranged in clusters ranging in size from 88 to 1024 GPUs.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/allenai/impactful-scheduling",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-09T15:20:29.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-11T12:28:11.769Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E3",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "These clusters are built for large-scale distributed training of AI models, and they serve a group of about 150 internal researchers whose work covers a diverse set of AI domains, including the full model flow of LLM and VLM training, robotics reinforcement learning (RL) simul…",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/allenai/impactful-scheduling",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-09T15:20:29.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-11T12:28:11.769Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E4",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Based on submitted workloads, at any moment in time we have outstanding requests for 2-3x more GPUs than are available.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/allenai/impactful-scheduling",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-09T15:20:29.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-11T12:28:11.769Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E5",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "One way to think about this is that every available GPU hour on our cluster has 2-3 different research workloads competing for it.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/allenai/impactful-scheduling",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-09T15:20:29.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-11T12:28:11.769Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E6",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "For example, we observed instances of GPU “squatting” where users would park no-op workloads they could connect to when the need arose.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/allenai/impactful-scheduling",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-09T15:20:29.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-11T12:28:11.769Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E7",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "We also observed priority inflation, where eventually 100% of scheduled workloads used HIGH priority.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/allenai/impactful-scheduling",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-09T15:20:29.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-11T12:28:11.769Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E8",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Our initial attempts to ensure the most important work received GPU time were focused on tighter control of how priorities were set, and, ultimately, working around the priority-based scheduler by explicitly assigning GPU monopolies to important projects.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/allenai/impactful-scheduling",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-09T15:20:29.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-11T12:28:11.769Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E9",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "For example, in their 2011 paper introducing Dominant Resource Fairness , Ghodsi et al. recount an anecdote in which a search company provided dedicated machines to jobs only if their users could guarantee high utilization.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/allenai/impactful-scheduling",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-09T15:20:29.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-11T12:28:11.769Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E10",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Before rolling out the budget-based system, we wanted a fast way to predict where those longer wait times might arise and to test configuration knobs like the length of the lookback window or the maximum value to allow for minimum runtime (we chose 8 hours).",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/allenai/impactful-scheduling",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-09T15:20:29.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-11T12:28:11.769Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E11",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Over the 30-day test period, teams were delivered 98% of the GPU hours they were owed, and 13 of 15 team allocations received 95% or more with the worst case receiving 90%.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/allenai/impactful-scheduling",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-09T15:20:29.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-11T12:28:11.769Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E12",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "18% of delivered GPU time was unallocated, which is how we maintained high occupancy during periods when funded use cases were not ready to run.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/allenai/impactful-scheduling",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-09T15:20:29.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-11T12:28:11.769Z"
      }
    ],
